      A border representation of a trust level boundary.
    </a:Description><a:Hidden>false</a:Hidden><a:Id>SE.TB.B.TrustLevel</a:Id><a:ImageLocation i:nil="true"/><a:ImageSource>/Images/ImageTrustLevelBoundary7.png</a:ImageSource><a:ImageStream i:nil="true"/><a:Name>Trust Level Boundary </a:Name><a:ParentId>GE.TB.B</a:ParentId><a:Representation>Inherited</a:Representation><a:Shape i:nil="true"/><a:StencilConstraints/></a:ElementType></a:StandardElements><a:ThreatCategories><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>S</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Spoofing</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>T</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Tampering</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>R</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Repudiation</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>I</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Information Disclosure</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Information disclosure happens when the information can be read by an unauthorized party.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>D</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Denial Of Service</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>E</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>P</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Privacy</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>A</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Abuse</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Abuse is when a legitimate user violates the terms of use for the system without violating a system security policy.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory></a:ThreatCategories><a:ThreatMetaData><IsPriorityUsed>true</IsPriorityUsed><IsStatusUsed>true</IsStatusUsed><PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Title</Name><Label>Title</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id i:nil="true"/><AttributeType>0</AttributeType></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatCategory</Name><Label>Category</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values i:nil="true" xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"/><Id i:nil="true"/><AttributeType>0</AttributeType></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id i:nil="true"/><AttributeType>0</AttributeType></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id i:nil="true"/><AttributeType>0</AttributeType></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>StateInformation</Name><Label>Justification</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id i:nil="true"/><AttributeType>0</AttributeType></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>InteractionString</Name><Label>Interaction</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values i:nil="true" xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"/><Id i:nil="true"/><AttributeType>0</AttributeType></ThreatMetaDatum></PropertiesMetaData></a:ThreatMetaData><a:ThreatTypes><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>Threat was migrated from V3.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'ROOT'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>SU</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Spoofing (v3)</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Threat was migrated from V3.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'ROOT'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>TU</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Tampering (v3)</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>R</a:Category><a:Description>Threat was migrated from V3.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'ROOT'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>RU</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Repudiation (v3)</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Threat was migrated from V3.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'ROOT'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>IU</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Information Disclosure (v3)</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>Threat was migrated from V3.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'ROOT'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>DU</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Denial Of Service (v3)</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>Threat was migrated from V3.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'ROOT'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>EU</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Elevation Of Privilege (v3)</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>{source.Name} may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to {target.Name}. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source process.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.authenticatesSource is 'Yes' or source.implementsAuthenticationScheme is 'Yes'</a:Exclude><a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and (target is 'GE.P' or target is 'GE.DS') and flow crosses 'GE.TB'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>S1</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Spoofing of a Source Process</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to information disclosure by {source.Name}. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source process.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.authenticatesDestination is 'Yes'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'GE.P' or source is 'GE.EI' or source is 'GE.DS') and target is 'GE.P' and flow crosses 'GE.TB'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>S2</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Spoofing of a Destination Process</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>{source.Name} may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to {target.Name}. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>source.authenticatesItself is 'Yes' or flow.authenticatesSource is 'Yes'</a:Exclude><a:Include>source is 'GE.EI' and target is 'GE.P'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>S3</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Spoofing of an External Entity</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>{source.Name} may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to incorrect data delivered to {target.Name}. Consider Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source data store.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.DS'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>S7</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Spoofing of a Source Data Store</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being written to the attacker's target instead of {target.Name}. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination data store.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>target is 'GE.DS'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>S7.1</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Spoofing of a Destination Data Store</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being sent to the attacker's target instead of {target.Name}. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.EI' and flow crosses 'GE.TB'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>S8</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Spoofing of an External Destination Entity</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Data flowing across {flow.Name} may be tampered by an attacker. This may lead to a denial of service attack against {target.Name} or an elevation of privilege attack against {target.Name} or an information disclosure by {target.Name}. Failure to verify that input is as expected is a root cause of a very large number of exploitable issues. Consider all paths and the way they handle data. Verify that all input is verified for correctness using a white list input validation approach.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>(source is 'GE.P' or source is 'GE.EI') and target is 'GE.P' and (flow crosses 'GE.TB')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T1</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Input Validation Failure</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>If {source.Name} is given access to memory, such as shared memory or pointers, or is given the ability to control what {target.Name} executes (for example, passing back a function pointer.), then {source.Name} can tamper with the {target.Name}. Consider if the function could work with less access to memory, such as passing data, rather than pointers. Copy in data provided, and then validate it.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.P' and target.codeType is 'Unmanaged'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T2</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Process Memory Tampered</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Packets without sequence numbers or timestamps can be captured and replayed in a wide variety of ways. Use an anti-replay technique (investigate sequence numbers before timers) and a strong integrity technique.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.P' and source.implementsCommunicationProtocol is 'Yes'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T3</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Packet Replay Attacks</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Attackers who can send a series of packets can overlap data. For example, packet 1 may be 100 bytes starting at offset 0. Packet 2 may be 100 bytes starting at offset 25. Packet 2 will overwrite 75 bytes of packet 1. Ensure you reassemble data before filtering it, and ensure you explicitly handle these sorts of cases. A variant might be allowing offsets to be signed.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.P' and source.implementsCommunicationProtocol is 'Yes'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T4</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Packet Collision Attacks</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Do your log readers understand the security aspects of your logs? Log readers have come under attack via log files. Consider ways to canonicalize data in the logs, and communicate with your log readers about what security assurances you offer. Consider truncating long user input. Ensure that if you have a single reader for the logs, they know where each field comes from, and which are untrustworthy. If you have many, ensure that you document what you do and don't do, so they can figure out where each field comes from.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.DS' and target.storesLogData is 'Yes'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T5</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Risks from Logging</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker can read or modify data transmitted over an authenticated dataflow.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(flow.providesConfidentiality is 'Yes' and flow.providesIntegrity is 'Yes')</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow.authenticatesSource is 'Yes' or flow.authenticatesDestination is 'Yes' or flow.transmitsCredentials is 'Yes')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T6</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Authenticated Data Flow Compromised</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>SQL injection is an attack in which malicious code is inserted into strings that are later passed to an instance of SQL Server for parsing and execution. Any procedure that constructs SQL statements should be reviewed for injection vulnerabilities because SQL Server will execute all syntactically valid queries that it receives. Even parameterized data can be manipulated by a skilled and determined attacker.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>
        (target is 'SE.DS.SQL' and source is 'GE.P')
      </a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T7</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>SQL Injection</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>SQL injection is an attack in which malicious code is inserted into strings that are later passed to an instance of SQL Server for parsing and execution. Any procedure that constructs SQL statements should be reviewed for injection vulnerabilities because SQL Server will execute all syntactically valid queries that it receives. Even parameterized data can be manipulated by a skilled and determined attacker.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>
        (target is 'SE.DS.SQL' and source is 'GE.EI')
      </a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T8</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>SQL Injection</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>XML injection is an attack in which malicious code is inserted into strings that are later parsed and executed. Any procedure that constructs XML data  should be reviewed for injection vulnerabilities.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>
        (target is 'SE.DS.XML' and source is 'GE.P')
      </a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T9</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>XML Injection</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>XML injection is an attack in which malicious code is inserted into strings that are later parsed and executed. Any procedure that constructs XML data  should be reviewed for injection vulnerabilities.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>
        (target is 'SE.DS.XML' and source is 'GE.EI')
      </a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T10</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>XML Injection</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>if a dataflow contains XML, XML processing threats (DTD and XSLT code execution) may be exploited.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>(flow.XMLenc is 'Yes' and target is 'GE.P')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T11</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>XML DTD and XSLT Processing</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>if a dataflow contains JSON, JSON processing and hijacking threats may be exploited.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>((flow is 'SE.DF.HTTP' or flow is 'SE.DF.HTTPS') and flow.JSON is 'Yes' and target is 'GE.P')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T12</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>JavaScript Object Notation Processing</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>The web server '{target.Name}' could be a subject to a cross-site scripting attack because it does not implement client input sanitizers.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>target.hasInputSanitizers is 'Yes'</a:Exclude><a:Include>target is 'SE.P.WebServer'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T13.1</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Cross Site Scripting</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>The web server '{target.Name}' could be a subject to a persistent cross-site scripting attack because it does not implement data store '{source.Name}' input and output sanitizers.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>target.hasOutputSanitizers is 'Yes'</a:Exclude><a:Include>target is 'SE.P.WebServer' and source is 'GE.DS'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T13.2</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Persistent Cross Site Scripting</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Removable storage may be arbitrarily written by an attacker. Subsequent usage of this data by an unsuspecting device may compromise it. Consider encrypting the data.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(target.Signed is 'Yes')</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'SE.P.Device' and target is 'SE.DS.RemStr')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T14</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Removable Mobile Storage Tampering</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>If the mobile device uses Bluetooth, external attackers may pair with the device and can drive input unbeknown to the user. </a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>(source is 'GE.EI' and target is 'SE.P.Device' and flow.channel is 'Bluetooth')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T15</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Bluetooth Data Tampering</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Mobile devices may be updated or compromised via SMS push functionality. </a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.Device' and target.SMSPush is 'Yes')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T16</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>SMS Push to Mobile Device</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Data flowing across {flow.Name} may be tampered by an attacker. This may lead to a corruption on {target.Name}. Ensure the integrity of the data flow to the data store.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>(source is 'GE.P' or source is 'GE.EI') and target is 'GE.DS' and (flow crosses 'GE.TB')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>T18</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Data Store Corrupted</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>R</a:Category><a:Description>If you have trust levels, is anyone other outside of the highest trust level allowed to log? Letting everyone write to your logs can lead to repudiation problems. Only allow trusted code to log.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>(source is 'GE.P' or source is 'GE.EI') and (target is 'GE.DS') and (target.storesLogData is 'Yes')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>R1</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Lower Trusted Subject Updates Logs</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>R</a:Category><a:Description>Do you accept logs from unknown or weakly authenticated users or systems? Identify and authenticate the source of the logs before accepting them.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>(source is 'GE.P' or source is 'GE.EI') and (target is 'GE.DS') and (target.storesLogData is 'Yes')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>R2</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Data Logs from an Unknown Source</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>R</a:Category><a:Description>Does the log capture enough data to understand what happened in the past? Do your logs capture enough data to understand an incident after the fact? Is such capture lightweight enough to be left on all the time? Do you have enough data to deal with repudiation claims? Make sure you log sufficient and appropriate data to handle a repudiation claims. You might want to talk to an audit expert as well as a privacy expert about your choice of data.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.DS' and target.storesLogData is 'Yes'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>R3</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Insufficient Information Audited</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>R</a:Category><a:Description>Consider what happens when the audit mechanism comes under attack, including attempts to destroy the logs, or attack log analysis programs. Ensure access to the log is through a reference monitor, which controls read and write separately. Document what filters, if any, readers can rely on, or writers should expect</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.DS' and target.storesLogData is 'Yes'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>R4</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Audit Data Weakly Protected</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>R</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>target is 'GE.P' and flow crosses 'GE.TB'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>R6</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Received Data Repudiated</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>R</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} claims that it did not receive data from a process on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>target is 'GE.EI' and flow crosses 'GE.TB'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>R7</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>External Entity Denies Receiving Data</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>R</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} claims that it did not write data received from an entity on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>target is 'GE.DS' and flow crosses 'GE.TB'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>R8</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Data Store Denies Writing Data</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Side channels are things that a system does that may reveal information about cryptographic operation such as files, temp files, globally visible mutexes, power consumption, noise, CPU heat etc. Side channel attacks examine these to glean information about the system that can then be used to compromise it. Review the side channels.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>(source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.DS' and source.implementsCryptography is 'Yes') or (source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.P' and target.implementsCryptography is 'Yes')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I1</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Side Channel Attacks</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Can you access {target.Name} and bypass the permissions for the object? For example by editing the files directly with a hex editor, or reaching it via filesharing? Ensure that your program is the only one that can access the data, and that all other subjects have to use your interface.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.DS' and source.implementsCustomAuthorizationMechanism is 'Yes'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I2</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Authorization Bypass</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Is there a plan for protecting the data? If not, is this by design? Ensure that each object is well protected and if you have objects which aren't protected, document what objects are unprotected and why and ensure it complies with the security policy and make sure your users are aware of that. Consider the case of a user with less permissions than the app and what happens if they can alter the data store directly. Consider if other consumers of the data store such as indexers or search apps have the appropriate permissions</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.DS' and not source.implementsCustomAuthorizationMechanism is 'Yes' and 
               (target.MaxDataSensitivity is 'MBI' or target.MaxDataSensitivity is 'HBI' or target.MaxDataSensitivity is 'Compliance')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I3</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Sensitive Data Disclosure</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Is transient and persistent storage initialized before use? If data is not, it may contain data from a previous allocation that may be disclosed to an attacker. </a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.DS'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I5</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Improper Resource Allocation and Deallocation</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Data flowing across {flow.Name} may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.providesConfidentiality is 'Yes'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'GE.P' or source is 'GE.EI') and target is 'GE.P' or (source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.DS')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I6</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Data Flow Sniffing</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker can read unprotected HBI data transmitted over {flow.Name}. Consider encrypting the data flow.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.providesConfidentiality is 'Yes' and flow.providesIntegrity is 'Yes'</a:Exclude><a:Include>flow.MaxDataSensitivity is 'HBI'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I7</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Lack of Protection for HBI</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker can read unprotected MBI data transmitted over {flow.Name}. Consider encrypting the data flow.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(flow.providesConfidentiality is 'Yes' and flow.providesIntegrity is 'Yes')</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow.MaxDataSensitivity is 'MBI' and flow crosses 'GE.TB')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I8</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Lack of Protection for MBI</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker can read HBI or Compliance data from {target.Name}. Consider encrypting the data source and data flows from it.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(target.Encrypted is 'Yes')</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'GE.DS' and (target.maxDataSensitivity is 'HBI' or target.maxDataSensitivity is 'Compliance'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I9</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>HBI or Compliance Data Disclosure</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>The security protections of '{flow.Name}' are inadequate for '{source.Name}'.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((flow.providesConfidentiality is 'Yes') and (flow.providesIntegrity is 'Yes'))</a:Exclude><a:Include>
        (
        source is 'GE.DS' and
        (
        ((source.maxDataSensitivity is 'HBI') or (source.maxDataSensitivity is 'Compliance'))
        and
        ((flow.maxDataSensitivity is 'MBI') or (flow.maxDataSensitivity is 'LBI') or (flow.MaxDataSensitivity is 'Public'))
        or
        (source.maxDataSensitivity is 'MBI')
        and
        ((flow.maxDataSensitivity is 'LBI') or (flow.MaxDataSensitivity is 'Public'))
        or
        (source.maxDataSensitivity is 'LBI')
        and
        (flow.MaxDataSensitivity is 'Public')
        ))
      </a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I10</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Source Offers Weaker Communications than Destination Requires</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>The security protections of '{flow.Name}' are inadequate for '{target.Name}'.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((flow.providesConfidentiality is 'Yes') and (flow.providesIntegrity is 'Yes'))</a:Exclude><a:Include>
        (
        (target is 'GE.DS') and
        (
        (((target.maxDataSensitivity is 'HBI') or (target.maxDataSensitivity is 'Compliance'))
        and
        ((flow.maxDataSensitivity is 'MBI') or (flow.maxDataSensitivity is 'LBI') or (flow.MaxDataSensitivity is 'Public')))
        or
        ((target.maxDataSensitivity is 'MBI')
        and
        ((flow.maxDataSensitivity is 'LBI') or (flow.MaxDataSensitivity is 'Public')))
        or
        ((target.maxDataSensitivity is 'LBI')
        and
        (flow.MaxDataSensitivity is 'Public'))
        ))
      </a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I11</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Destination Offers Weaker Communications than Source Requires</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>If applications or services store information in '{source.Name}' HTML5 local storage, this information may be subject to unauthorized disclosure and modification.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(source.Encrypted is 'Yes' and source.Signed is 'Yes')</a:Exclude><a:Include>
        (source is 'SE.DS.HTML5LS' and
        (source.MaxDataSensitivity is 'HBI' or source.MaxDataSensitivity is 'Compliance' or source.MaxDataSensitivity is 'MBI'))
      </a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I12</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Cross-domain Information Disclosure through HTML5 Local Storage</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>If applications or services store information in '{target.Name}' HTML5 local storage, this information may be subject to unauthorized disclosure and modification.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(target.Encrypted is 'Yes' and target.Signed is 'Yes')</a:Exclude><a:Include>
        (target is 'SE.DS.HTML5LS' and
        (target.MaxDataSensitivity is 'HBI' or target.MaxDataSensitivity is 'Compliance' or target.MaxDataSensitivity is 'MBI'))
      </a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I13</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Cross-domain Information Disclosure through HTML5 Local Storage</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>If information above LBI is stored in cookies, this information in '{source.Name}' may be subject to unauthorized disclosure and modification, particularly from JavaScript.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(source.Encrypted is 'Yes' and source.HTTPonly is 'Yes')</a:Exclude><a:Include>
        (source is 'SE.DS.Cookie' and
        (source.MaxDataSensitivity is 'HBI' or source.MaxDataSensitivity is 'Compliance' or source.MaxDataSensitivity is 'MBI'))
      </a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I14</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Information Disclosure through Local Cookies</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>If information above LBI is stored in cookies, this information in '{target.Name}' may be subject to unauthorized disclosure and modification, particularly from JavaScript.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(target.Encrypted is 'Yes' and target.HTTPonly is 'Yes')</a:Exclude><a:Include>
        (target is 'SE.DS.Cookie' and
        (target.MaxDataSensitivity is 'HBI' or target.MaxDataSensitivity is 'Compliance' or target.MaxDataSensitivity is 'MBI'))
      </a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I15</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Information Disclosure through Local Cookies</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Mobile devices may contain sensitive user information, which may be read by an attacker from the device file system via DMA or direct physical attacks. Consider encrypting the user data on the device.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(target.Encrypted is 'Yes' or target.Authenticated is 'Yes')</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.DS.Device')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I16</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Theft or Loss of User Data on Mobile Device</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Removable storage devices are vulnerable to loss or theft, which may compromise the data on the lost storage. Consider encrypting the data on the device.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(target.Encrypted is 'Yes')</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'SE.P.Device' and target is 'SE.DS.RemStr')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I17</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Theft or Loss of User Data on Removable Devices</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Devices connecting to Wi-Fi access points could result in snooping, tampering, and spoofing by the entity that controls the access point. </a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>((source is 'SE.P.Device') and ((target is 'GE.P') or (target is 'GE.DS')) and (flow.channel is 'WiFi'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I18</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Wi-Fi Access Point Compromised</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Mobile devices connecting to network base stations could result in snooping, tampering, and spoofing by the entity that controls the base station. </a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>((source is 'SE.P.Device') and ((target is 'GE.P') or (target is 'GE.DS')) and (flow.channel is '2G-4G'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I19</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Carrier Base Station Compromised</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>MMobile devices with GPS sensors can be aware of that device's location, which could be  disclosed to an unauthorized third party. Applications should be implemented using the fewest privileges needed to realize the scenario.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.Device' and target.GPS is 'Yes')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I21</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Physical Location Disclosed by Application</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Improper data protection of {source.name} can allow an attacker to read information not intended for disclosure. Review authorization settings.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.DS' and (target is 'GE.P' or target is 'GE.EI')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I23</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Weak Access Control for a Resource</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Credentials held at the server are often disclosed or tampered with and credentials stored on the client are often stolen. For server side, consider authentication that doesn't store secrets on the server (for example, public key.). If storing shared secrets, hash or encrypt them according to requirements. Ensure there is a "salt". Consider not storing the credentials. For client side, if storing credentials is required, encrypt them and protect the file in which they're stored</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.DS' and target.storesCredentials is 'Yes'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I24</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Weak Credential Storage</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Credentials on the wire are often subject to sniffing by an attacker. Are the credentials re-usable/re-playable? Are credentials included in a message? For example, sending a zip file with the password in the email. Use strong cryptography for the transmission of credentials. Use the OS libraries if at all possible, and consider cryptographic algorithm agility, rather than hardcoding a choice.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow is 'SE.DF.HTTPS' or flow is 'SE.DF.IPSec'</a:Exclude><a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and (target is 'GE.P' or target is 'GE.DS') and (flow crosses 'SE.TB.L.Machine' or flow crosses 'SE.TB.B.Machine')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I25</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Weak Credential Transit</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Custom authentication schemes are susceptible to common weaknesses such as weak credential change management, credential equivalence, easily guessable credentials, null credentials, downgrade authentication or a weak credential change management system. Consider the impact and potential mitigations for your custom authentication scheme.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.P' and source.implementsAuthenticationScheme is 'Yes'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>I26</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Weak Authentication Scheme</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>Does {source.Name} or {target.Name} take explicit steps to control resource consumption? Resource consumption attacks can be hard to deal with, and there are times that it makes sense to let the OS do the job. Be careful that your resource requests don't deadlock, and that they do timeout.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.DS'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>D2</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Excessive Resource Consumption</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} crashes, halts, stops or runs slowly; in all cases violating an availability metric.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>target is 'GE.P' and flow crosses 'GE.TB'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>D3</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Process Crash or Stop</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>An external threat agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>flow crosses 'GE.TB'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>D4</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Network Data Flow Interrupted</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>An external threat agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>source is 'GE.DS' or target is 'GE.DS'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>D5</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Data Store Inaccessible</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>Links to untrusted sites (such as advertising networks) are a major vulnerability source for web sites, particularly if XSS issues are present. Flag such potential vulnerabilities.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(source.MaxDataSensitivity is target.MaxTrustLevel 
               or 
                  source.MaxDataSensitivity is 'MBI' 
                  and 
                  (target.MaxTrustLevel is 'HBI' or target.MaxTrustLevel is 'Compliance') 
               or 
                  source.MaxDataSensitivity is 'LBI' 
                  and 
                  (target.MaxTrustLevel is 'MBI' or target.MaxTrustLevel is 'HBI' or target.MaxTrustLevel is 'Compliance') 
               or 
                  source.MaxDataSensitivity is 'Public' 
                  and 
                  (target.MaxTrustLevel is 'LBI' or target.MaxTrustLevel is 'MBI' or target.MaxTrustLevel is 'HBI' or target.MaxTrustLevel is 'Compliance')
      )</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'SE.P.WebServer' and (target is 'SE.EI.WebApp' or target is 'SE.EI.WebSvc'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>E1</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Untrusted URLs</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>Common SSO implementations such as OAUTH2 and OAUTH Wrap are vulnerable to MitM attacks.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(target is 'SE.EI.AuthProvider' and target.MS is 'Yes')</a:Exclude><a:Include>target is 'SE.EI.AuthProvider'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>E3</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Weakness in SSO Authorization</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} may be able to impersonate the context of {source.Name} in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>(source is 'GE.EI' or source is 'GE.P') and target is 'GE.P'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>E5</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} may be able to remotely execute code for {source.Name}.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>target is 'GE.P' and flow crosses 'GE.TB'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>E6</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Elevation Using Remote Code Execution</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker may pass data into {target.Name} in order to change the flow of program execution within {target.Name} to the attacker's choosing.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude/><a:Include>target is 'GE.P' and flow crosses 'GE.TB'</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>E7</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData/><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in the Destination Process</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType></a:ThreatTypes></KnowledgeBase><Profile><PromptedKb xmlns=""/></Profile></ThreatModel>